	Let $ F:V \to W $ be a linear map whose kernel is $ \{\vec{0} \} $. If $ \vec{v}_1,\cdots,\vec{v}_n $ are linearly independent elements of $ V $, then $ F(\vec{v}_1),\cdots,F(\vec{v}_n) $ are linearly independent elements of $ W $.
